Your taskmasters soon organise labour camps outside of the gate of St. Romanos where the refugees are used to cut down timber from the neighbouring Veligrádio forest. Anyone who wants to enter through the gate, must also bring some timber or stone from the local quarry. Not everyone is physically fit enough to participate in this labour and many thousands of refugees instead choose to depart elsewhere. The people feel that this is a harsh decision, but nobles, priests and soldiers understand that this is a necessary measure for the safety of the City. \[Public Morale -10\] \[Materials are now {GetInt("iMaterials")} \] \[City Population is now {GetPopulation()} \]

Soon brigands and mercenaries of all kinds flock to our banner. Primarily they are Italians from various states, but Cumans also come, Bulgars and even some Turks. They are not very numerous, but they are hardened killers, veterans of many wars, so their presence raises the quality of your troops across the board. However, their presence, unfamiliar tongues and strange customs unnerve your people, priests, nobles and even other troops. In total, 750 infantry, 750 archers and 100 cavalry join your ranks. \[Infantry +750\] \[Archers +750\] \[Cavalry +100\] \[Noble Support -5\] \[Priest Support -5\] \[Troop Morale -5\] \[Public Morale -5\] \[Infantry Quality is increased\] \[Archers Quality is increased\] \[Cavalry Quality is increased\]
